#: ../../source/user-guide/metrics/health_metrics.md:39
msgid ""
"Use the Gauge to determine whether a Store is currently fused. Use both "
"the success and failure Counters to analyze probe quality over time. "
"There is currently no dedicated Counter for fuse or recovery transitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/metrics/health_metrics.md:41
msgid ""
"Metric names distinguish Store types, while labels distinguish vLLM "
"instances and UCM processes. Connector metrics carry `model_name`, "
"`engine`, and `worker_rank`; Prometheus also adds `job` and `instance`. "
"See [UCM Metrics Observability](metrics.md) for the complete label "
"definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/metrics/health_metrics.md:43
msgid "2.1 Synchronization Delay in Connector Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/metrics/health_metrics.md:45
msgid ""
"The health threads continue to run inside UCM at their configured "
"interval, but connector metrics are synchronized to `/metrics` only when "
"vLLM calls `get_kv_connector_stats()`. With no inference requests, the "
"health metrics in Prometheus do not update even if the background probe "
"result has changed."
msgstr ""

